&lt;h2 id=&#34;contributing&#34;&gt;Contributing
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;We welcome contributions to Storybook!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📥 Pull requests and 🌟 Stars are always welcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read our &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;CONTRIBUTING.md&#34; &gt;contributing guide&lt;/a&gt; to get started,
or find us on &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://discord.gg/storybook&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Discord&lt;/a&gt;, we will take the time to guide you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Looking for a first issue to tackle?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We tag issues with &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook/issues?q=is%3Aopen&amp;#43;is%3Aissue&amp;#43;label%3A%22good&amp;#43;first&amp;#43;issue%22&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://img.shields.io/github/issues/storybookjs/storybook/good%20first%20issue.svg&#34;
	
	
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
		alt=&#34;Good First Issue&#34;
	
	
&gt;&lt;/a&gt; when we think they are well suited for people who are new to the codebase or OSS in general.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://discord.gg/storybook&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Talk to us&lt;/a&gt;, we&amp;rsquo;ll find something to suits your skills and learning interest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;development-scripts&#34;&gt;Development scripts
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Storybook is organized as a monorepo using &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://lerna.js.org/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Lerna&lt;/a&gt;. Useful scripts include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&#34;yarn-bootstrap&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;yarn bootstrap&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Installs package dependencies and links packages together - using lerna&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&#34;yarn-lint&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;yarn lint&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;boolean check if code conforms to linting rules - uses remark &amp;amp; eslint&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;yarn lint:js&lt;/code&gt; - will check js&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;yarn lint:md&lt;/code&gt; - will check markdown + code samples&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;yarn lint:js --fix&lt;/code&gt; - will automatically fix js&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&#34;yarn-test&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;yarn test&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;boolean check if unit tests all pass - uses jest&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;yarn run test --core --watch&lt;/code&gt; - will run core tests in watch-mode&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
